'''Working Dog Productions''' (originally '''Frontline Television Productions Pty Ltd''') is a film and television [[production company]] based in [[Melbourne]], Australia. It was formed in 1993 by actors [[Santo Cilauro]], [[Rob Sitch]], [[Jane Kennedy (actor)|Jane Kennedy]], [[Tom Gleisner]], and producer Michael Hirsh.

== History ==
[[File:Tom Gleisner, Rob Sitch, Michael Hirsh 2012 (1).jpg|thumb|Three of Working Dog's founders: [[Tom Gleisner]] (left), [[Rob Sitch]] (middle), and Michael Hirsh (right)]]
Frontline Television Productions Pty Ltd<ref name="SBS">{{cite web | last=Cassar | first=Jeremy | title=Working Dog: 30 years of biting at the cutting edge of comedy | website=sbs.com.au | date=7 October 2016 | url=https://www.sbs.com.au/guide/article/2016/10/07/working-dog-30-years-biting-cutting-edge-comedy | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210928023834/https://www.sbs.com.au/guide/article/2016/10/07/working-dog-30-years-biting-cutting-edge-comedy | archive-date=28 September 2021 | url-status=dead | access-date=3 August 2026}}</ref> was formed in 1993 by five collaborators who had worked together on earlier comedy projects, actors [[Santo Cilauro]], [[Rob Sitch]], [[Jane Kennedy (actor)|Jane Kennedy]], [[Tom Gleisner]], and producer Michael Hirsh.<ref name="SydneyMorningHerald">{{cite news|last=Enker|first=Debi|title=Utopia proves there's nothing else like a Working Dog formula|url=http://www.smh.com.au/entertainment/tv-and-radio/utopia-proves-theres-nothing-else-like-a-working-dog-formula-20140804-1004w2.html|newspaper=[[The Sydney Morning Herald]]|date=7 August 2014|access-date=1 November 2016}}</ref> The group of actors became known through their earlier hit comedy sketch show ''[[The D-Generation]]'' (1986–1987) and ''[[The Late Show (1992 TV series)|The Late Show]]'' (1992), forming their production company with producer Michael Hirsh before creating ''[[Frontline (Australian TV series)|Frontline]]'' under the banner of Working Dog.<ref name="SBS"/>

It adopted the name Working Dog Productions in the mid-1990s.<ref>{{Cite web |title=About Us – Working Dog |url=https://watch.workingdog.com/page/about-us/ |access-date=20 September 2025 |website=Working Dog Official}}</ref> The founders have described the company origin as "five friends formed a production company with a dodgy camcorder and a dream".<ref>{{Cite web |title=About Us – Working Dog |url=https://watch.workingdog.com/page/about-us/ |access-date=20 September 2025 |website=Working Dog Official}}</ref>

==Description==
Working Dog Productions is a film and television [[production company]] based in Melbourne, Victoria.<ref name="SBS"/>

The company name and mascot (an [[Australian Cattle Dog]]) reflect the founders' affection for dogs, and the company has retained the original creative core across decades while expanding into multi-platform production and a small executive/staff structure.<ref>{{Cite web |title= About Us |url=https://watch.workingdog.com/page/about-us/ |access-date=2025-09-20 |website=Working Dog On Demand |language=en}}</ref>

==Productions==
In addition to television and film, Working Dog Productions have also ventured into books, stage shows, and [[podcast]]s.<ref>{{cite web|title=Working Dog’s Pacific Heat to air on Foxtel November 27|url=http://if.com.au/2016/10/05/article/Working-Dogs-Pacific-Heat-to-air-on-Foxtel-November-27/PCLTGAHYUY.html|work=IF.com.au|date=6 October 2016|access-date=7 November 2016}}</ref>
